do we finally know what luffy's real  dream is not to become pirate king but  the one that hola sensei has only hinted  at in his flashback with sabo and ace  the exact same dream that also roger  hats and that inspired people like  crocus shanks and rayleigh to put all  their faith into a rubbery boy to change  the world well i think that chapter 1049  of one piece really seems to suggest so  at the climax of the epic battle between  luffy and kaido both of them attacking  with what seems like their last ultimate  techniques the emperor asks luffy what  kind of world he wants to make if he's  actually strong enough to change it and  in a series of three absolutely  incredible double spreads luffy replies  that he wants to make a world in which  his friends can eat and drink as much as  they wish  i can't even begin to explain the sort  of goosebumps that this gave me now why  do i think that this answer not only  makes a ton of sense but more  importantly also wonderfully embodies  the main theme and message of one piece  as a story because there is a lot packed  into this little statement one big  theory that i heard being thrown around  a while ago is that luffy's real dream  might be to have a giant banquet with  all of his friends based on the fact  that the end of every major arc and  victory for the crew kind of has luffy  celebrating it with a feast which  honestly i think was really close but  did not quite hit the mark because just  one giant banquet would imply that  luffy's biggest desire would be having  one giant event with all his friends  laughing and feasting together which i  absolutely do think will happen don't  get me wrong but it doesn't quite  address the main theme of the story  freedom the fact that luffy wants to  make a world where everyone can eat as  much as they want in friends and food  the two things that he loves the most in  this world implies that he wants him to  have the freedom to live the happiest  life that he can imagine in other words  to me it's kind of the most looty way of  saying that he wants to liberate the  world it takes luffy's biggest quirk as  a character eating like there is no  tomorrow and connecting it to the  central moral message of one piece which  i just found absolutely beautiful the  banquets that luffy had so far always  are a celebration of life among equals  that now are free to do whatever they  like eat drink sing dance because as we  know at this point luffy is basically  friends with everyone in the world  except those who stand in the way of  everyone else's happiness in a world  where most people live in poverty and  despair ruled by a small group of people  that have all the wealth and luxury i  would argue that means that luffy's goal  is to take down the world nobles and  free the world which ironically is  exactly what kaido's goal is who's  flashback by the way i'm just pumped to  discuss in just a moment of course as  well and so even more awesomely is  possibly a word  well now it is even more awesomely the  theme of eating and drinking as much as  one likes not only references the story  as a whole but of course also connects  wonderfully to the themes of wano in  particular as well a country that is  starving and has no clean water to drink  an arc that literally started with luffy  being gifted the little bit of thomas  rice that she actually had to eat and so  he shouts his dream for a better world  at the climax of the raid on onigishima  where kaido has been holding a yearly  banquet with all the food and all the  drinks anyone could want but only for  his men and those few who are actually  in power and so even though luffy and  kaido share the exact same goal in a way  freeing the world  kaido has taken the wrong path to get  there becoming what he hated the most in  the process don't you find it ironic as  well that we see kaido literally  declaring war on the nobles that took  away his freedom and that of the people  he loved by creating a de facto system  of world nobles inside mono itself  because that is kaido's big flaw as a  character that in the end only luffy  will be able to make him see and realize  it's actually very similar to big mom i  feel nada think about it because she has  created an actual country made out of  food also pretty much based on luffy's  dream only that here the people are of  course not really free to do whatever  they want and live a happy life though  let's be real it's a lot better than  wano indians and so two of the yonkos  have basically started where luffy did  only that where kylo and big mom lost  their course somewhere along the way and  turned into villains luffy will be the  one who actually succeeds in making this  stream a reality most importantly  without becoming the bad guy in the  process i mean that's what always has  made luffy special and why i love this  chapter and the reveal of luffy's actual  dream so so much also did you notice how  young big mom is very similar to young  luffy genuinely kind and caring or how  young kaido in this chapter basically  looks like a young luffy but with horns  and actually since we're on the topic  right now let me share my thoughts on  kaido's flashback that we got in this  chapter as well okay so as you will  notice i absolutely loved loved the  overall story of how kaido became the  person who is today and i will go into  detail here in just a moment but i do  have to get this one thing off my chest  first because if this is gonna be  everything that we're gonna get for his  past that would be way too short for me  personally at least this is the final  villain of not only the longest arc in  all of one piece but also the entire  yonko saga past the time skip i mean  kaido has gotten a ton of absolutely  next level character development during  onigishima but i just really really want  to see  more details and more interactions from  his past like at least an entire chapter  two or three or four i want to see more  of kaido interacting with young big mom  and white beards and i do get that oda  sensei is probably saving a lot of that  for when he's actually gonna reveal  rocks and his past but still i really  think that kaido is interesting and  important to the story right now not  like a hundred chapters from now and so  if this is it if this is all we're gonna  get  not quite long enough for me personally  i want to see more however that being  said what gives me a lot of hope  honestly that we will see a lot more  from kaido's past is the fact that we  still don't know a lot about for example  what he was experimented on how he  recruited the rest of his men how he  learned about joy boy in the first place  and so on and so forth so truly fingers  crossed or some more the flashback that  we did get so far though content-wise at  least was just so good  i mean i love the fact that kaido is  from a kingdom that's literally called  vodka given that he is a pretty bad  alcoholic how he made a name for himself  as his country's strongest warrior at  the age of 10 only to be sold after the  marines by the king for the chance to  get more power by getting access to the  referee he basically comes from an  island that did war and plundering as  its main job to raise enough money for  the heavenly tribute which is basically  protection money a country has to pay to  the world government to not be attacked  by them actually it kind of feels like  the world government is sort of a mafia  that runs the entire planet actually and  so this explains a lot of kaido's  character traits he has known nothing  but war ever since he was a little kid  really he has learned to hate the world  government as they're responsible for  his childhoods and being sold and  betrayed by his entire country i  absolutely love that oda sensei baited  us by saying that kaido was captured and  executed a bunch of times by the marines  but as it turns out most of the time he  just escaped and let himself be  recaptured whenever he became hungry  which is not only the most hilarious  explanation for the strongest creature  being captured that often but it also  ties in surprisingly nicely with the  food theme of luffy's dream again  another really interesting detail in  this entire thing i found was once again  big mom's interaction with kaido because  it really seems like these two used to  have a much closer relationship than we  originally thought linlin is almost  behaving like a big sister here and is  shocked to find out that kaido once  again vanished after rox was defeated by  garvin roger he vanishes a lot it seems  and again we still don't know how this  all played out but it sounds like at  least these two were pretty close even  after whatever went down at god valley  but in a way the most important reveal  in this entire chapter to me at least  was something that i had already been  speculating for quite a while now and  was nice to see confirmed because kaido  basically confirms to us that he's been  trying to bring about the return of joy  boy and while king thought that it would  be kaido himself kaido was waiting for  the one who could defeat him which is  why he was so disappointed at the  beginning that luffy couldn't defeat him  only that luffy came back not once not  twice but three times if i'm counting  correctly each time stronger and more  determined than before and the fact that  kaido remembers this conversation with  king at the moment that he's punched  down by luffy to me really shows that he  is almost relieved and happy that luffy  has delivered such a massive blow and  has been able to push him this far i  mean even the flame clouds have vanished  which by the way has finally triggered  momo into fully summoning clouds of his  own and so now the big question is of  course is kaido defeated or not while  all of this clearly sets up our  expectations for kaido being defeated  here and luffy having run out of steam  too i personally would like to think  that this fight isn't over i mean luffy  has come back a number of times in this  fight already but kaido hasn't had to  pull off a full comeback even once so  far i also still don't quite believe  that we've seen his awaken form yet and  i would honestly like this battle to  continue on for a little bit longer i  feel like kaido will stand back up at  some points however it doesn't  necessarily have to be against luffy  really i think the last panel shows us  that kaido has realized that luffy is  joy boy and is acknowledging his power  luffy has overcome him in this moment  and so i would absolutely love to see  kaido getting back up to defend luffy  against the government forces or  blackbeard or whoever it might be that  might try to take luffy out while they  still have the chance and so kaido  defending joyboy and inheriting his will  to free the world onto luffy would be a  fantastic redemption arc for his  character i think that for whatever  reason i really want to see for kaido  actually if you want to know why you  really can't ignore this analysis video  of kaido i've done and if you've enjoyed  this video why not subscribe to the  channel for more
 

